DESCRIPTION:All Saints' Day falls on November 1 in the Western churches and
  honors all the saints of the church\, both the named and the unknown\, wh
 o have attained heaven. The Eastern churches keep the same commemoration o
 n the first Sunday after Pentecost instead. Its origin cannot be traced wi
 th certainty\, and the November 1 date arrived long after the feast itself
  — by way of a Roman chapel dedication\, an English monk's calendar\, an
 d finally a papal order.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/all-saints
 -day/
